.TH SPECDD 1 "May 2026" "specdd 1.2.0" "SpecDD CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
specdd \- command-line tool for SpecDD workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B specdd
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B specdd init
.RI [ path ]
.RB [ --version
.IR version ]
.br
.B specdd update
.RB [ --version
.IR version ]
.br
.B specdd check-update
.br
.B specdd agentskills deploy
.RI [ path ]
.RB [ --user ]
.RB [ --version
.IR version ]
.br
.B specdd inspect
.RI [ path ]
.RB [ --section
.IR name ]
.RB [ --sections
.IR names ]
.RB [ --format
.IR format ]
.br
.B specdd plugin add
.I repository pluginname
.RI [ version ]
.br
.B specdd plugin list
.RB [ --output
.IR format ]
.br
.B specdd plugin update
.RI [ repository ]
.RI [ pluginname ]
.RI [ version ]
.br
.B specdd resolve
.I target
.RB [ --root
.IR path ]
.RB [ --section
.IR name ]
.RB [ --sections
.IR names ]
.RB [ --depth
.IR depth ]
.RB [ --format
.IR format ]
.br
.B specdd lint
.RI [ path ]
.RB [ --format
.IR format ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B specdd
is a command-line tool for working with SpecDD framework-enabled
projects. It initializes SpecDD project files, updates existing SpecDD
installations, checks for framework updates, deploys SpecDD Agent Skills,
installs, lists, and updates plugins,
and inspects, resolves, or lints local
.B .sdd
specification files.
.PP
SpecDD projects are driven by source-adjacent
.B .sdd
spec files.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [path]
Initialize SpecDD in the current directory or in
.IR path .
If the target directory does not exist,
.B init
creates it. SpecDD is added only when
.B .specdd/bootstrap.md
is not already present.
.TP
.B update
Update an existing SpecDD project. The current directory must contain
.B .specdd/bootstrap.md .
When using the default latest release,
.B update
compares the local bootstrap
.B Version
front matter with the latest release and does nothing when the local
version is already current or newer.
.TP
.B check-update
Print the local SpecDD version, if any, and the latest available release
version.
.TP
.B agentskills deploy [path]
Deploy SpecDD Agent Skills into a project directory. By default the
current directory is used. Project installs write to
.BR <project>/.agents/skills .
Only valid
.B specdd-*
skill directories that contain
.B SKILL.md
are installed.
.TP
.B inspect [path]
Discover
.B .sdd
files for a target path and print selected sections in a tree-shaped
report. If
.I path
is omitted, the current directory is inspected. The target may be a
directory, a
.B .sdd
file, or an ordinary file, and must exist.
Root-level project specs follow the containing directory basename
convention.
Directory blocks include parent-held directory specs such as
.B src/foo/bar.sdd
and local directory specs such as
.B src/foo/bar/bar.sdd
when both govern the same directory.
.TP
.B plugin add repository pluginname [version]
Install the repository file
.B .plugins/<pluginname>/plugin.md
into the current project, which must contain
.BR .specdd/bootstrap.md .
GitHub shorthand
.B @owner/repository
uses
.BR git@github.com:owner/repository.git .
SSH URLs, SCP-style SSH addresses, and explicit HTTPS URLs are supported.
SCP-style path segments are limited to ASCII letters, digits, dots,
underscores, and hyphens; percent escapes are rejected.
Git and an SSH client are required for SSH access. Authentication uses the
existing SSH agent and configuration; SSH failures do not fall back to HTTPS.
Only branches and tags and their history are fetched. The optional version
is an exact tag, branch, or commit identifier reachable from a branch or tag.
Pull-request refs and other ref namespaces are not fetched.
When omitted, the remote default branch is selected and the registry records
.BR latest .
An explicit
.B latest
selects that Git ref. Ambiguous branch/tag names fail; use
.B refs/heads/<name>
or
.B refs/tags/<name>
to disambiguate.
.PP
Plugins are stored at
.BR .specdd/plugins/<host>/<namespace>/<repository>/<pluginname>/plugin.md .
Coordinates omit the terminal
.B .git
suffix and retain nested namespaces. A nondefault port uses
.BR <host>~<port> .
The registry at
.B .specdd/plugins.json
is an array of objects with string fields
.BR src ,
.BR origin ,
.BR sig ,
and
.BR version .
Generated sources are relative to the registry directory. Existing sources
may be absolute, relative, or start with a home-directory
.BR ~ .
Origin records the repository address and resolved commit separated by
.BR # .
It preserves the repository path and any
.B .git
suffix, removing passwords and HTTPS user information.
Sig is the lowercase SHA-256 of the exact installed bytes; version preserves
the supplied version or defaults to
.BR latest .
.PP
Repeated additions update the existing registration. Identical content and
metadata are unchanged. Locally modified and unregistered destination files
are preserved with an error. Missing registered files may be restored.
Changes to the target registration during download, verification, or
confirmation cancel the operation, including otherwise unchanged installations.
Unrelated entries are preserved. Malformed registries, duplicate source paths,
and redirected symlink writes are rejected. Registry write failures roll back
the installed file; rollback failures identify the affected path.
Concurrent installs fail while
.B .specdd/plugins.lock
is held. After forcible termination, confirm no installation is running
before removing a stale lock and verify the file against its recorded checksum.
Expected plugin installation failures exit with status 1.
.PP
An optional detached OpenPGP signature at
.B .plugins/<pluginname>/plugin.md.asc
is read from the same resolved commit as the plugin. Valid signatures from
bundled, fingerprint-pinned SpecDD vendor keys are accepted automatically.
Every repository under
.B github.com/specdd/
requires verification against those embedded keys, including shorthand such as
.BR @specdd/plugins ,
SSH, and HTTPS inputs. Hostname and organization matching is case-insensitive.
Missing, invalid, expired, revoked, or non-vendor signatures for official
sources fail with an error and exit status 1, without system-key fallback or
a confirmation override. This applies to additions, unchanged installations,
and updates.
.PP
For other repositories, signatures outside the bundled keys are checked using the optional
.B gpg
executable and the current user's keyring, including
.BR GNUPGHOME .
Full or ultimate identity validity is required for automatic acceptance.
Keys are not retrieved or imported, and trust settings are not changed.
.PP
For these other repositories, missing or unverifiable signatures produce a warning and
.BR "Continue? [y/N]" ,
defaulting to No. Valid signatures with insufficient identity validity receive
a separate warning with the full signing fingerprint and validity; never-valid
identities are explicitly reported as untrusted. Expired and revoked keys
receive specific warnings. Continue only after independently confirming that
the key belongs to a vendor you trust. Only case-insensitive y or yes permits
installation. Refusal, cancellation, or noninteractive input/output exits with
status 1 without modifying the plugin or registry. Required warnings are not
filtered by log_level. Repeated additions, including unchanged installations,
require the same verification. The registry checksum is separate from
publisher signature verification. GnuPG must be installed separately for
system-key verification, including in custom container images; interactive
Docker confirmation requires a terminal, for example docker run -it.
.TP
.B plugin list
List registrations from the current directory's
.B .specdd/plugins.json
in registry order. Text shows each source path, version, origin, and SHA-256
checksum. Source spelling is preserved, including absolute, relative, and
home-directory paths. Registrations are listed even when their files are
unavailable; listing does not verify files or contact Git repositories.
.PP
A missing registry or empty array produces
.B No plugins installed.
in text or an empty plugins array in JSON, with exit status 0.
No bootstrap file is required and no files are created.
Invalid output formats and unreadable or malformed registries exit with status 1.
.TP
.B plugin update [repository] [pluginname] [version]
Update all managed plugins with no arguments, or select a repository and
plugin name together with an optional version override. Repository inputs
and plugin names follow the same rules as
.BR "plugin add" ,
including GitHub shorthand, SSH addresses, and HTTPS URLs. Equivalent
repository URLs select the same canonical repository-and-plugin coordinate.
Only registrations whose resolved source is beneath the current project's
.B .specdd/plugins/
directory are selected. External registrations and files are untouched.
The plugin name comes from the directory containing
.BR plugin.md ,
and the source must match the recorded repository's managed installation path.
Absolute, relative, and home-directory source spelling is preserved.
.PP
Fetch from the Git repository recorded in
.B origin
using the recorded
.BR version .
The origin commit fragment records provenance and does not pin the update.
A recorded
.B latest
tracks the remote default branch. Other recorded versions retain their exact
tag, branch, or commit value. A supplied version overrides and replaces the
named plugin's recorded version. An explicit
.B latest
selects that Git ref; use
.B refs/tags/latest
or
.B refs/heads/latest
to retain that selection on future updates. Existing SSH agent authentication
and Git configuration apply. Fetching uses the recorded origin and transport,
even if an equivalent transport URL was supplied as the selector.
.PP
An uninstalled repository-and-plugin coordinate fails before downloading.
Plugins with the same name in other repositories are left untouched.
A bare plugin name or repository is rejected; supply both or neither.
No managed registrations produces
.B No managed plugins installed.
and exit status 0 without creating files. Updating an installed plugin
requires the project's bootstrap file.
.PP
Preserve registry order, source spelling, and additional metadata, while
refreshing origin, checksum, and version. Signature verification and
confirmation, checksum, symlink, locking, and
rollback protections from installation remain active. A registration changed
after selection, including during verification or confirmation, is rejected.
Validate all selected source metadata before
installation; process plugins in registry order and stop on the first failure.
Earlier successful updates remain installed. Success exits with status 0;
expected failures exit with status 1.
.TP
.B resolve target
Resolve specs relevant to
.IR target ,
where
.I target
is a directory,
.B .sdd
file, or ordinary file. The target must exist. Resolution always
includes vertical directory context from the
target up to the root, and then expands soft links from the target and
nearby parent context specs.
Non-glob directory links resolve to directory-level specs for that
directory; use a glob to include descendant specs.
Ordinary file targets use a same-basename
.B .sdd
file as the target anchor when present.
Vertical context uses the same cumulative parent-held and local
directory spec layout as
.BR inspect .
.TP
.B lint [path]
Lint
.B .sdd
files for a target path. If
.I path
is omitted, the current directory is linted. The target may be a
directory, a
.B .sdd
file, or an ordinary file, and must exist. Text output prints only files
with diagnostics.
Lint JSON uses the same cumulative directory spec layout as
.BR inspect .
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.TP
.BI --version " version"
Use a specific SpecDD release version for commands that download SpecDD
release assets. Versions use dotted numeric values such as
.B 1.2
or
.BR 1.2.3 ,
without a leading
.BR v .
.SH AGENT SKILLS OPTIONS
.TP
.B --user
Install Agent Skills into the current user's Agent Skills directory,
.BR ~/.agents/skills .
This option cannot be combined with a project target path.
.TP
.BI --version " version"
Install a specific Agent Skills release tag.
.SH INSPECT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --section " name"
Include a section by name, or
.BR all .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI --sections " names"
Include comma-separated section names, for example
.BR Purpose,Must,Tasks .
Use
.B all
to include every SpecDD section present in each spec.
.TP
.BI --format " format"
Set output format. Supported values are
.BR text ,
.BR json ,
and
.BR json-extended .
The default is
.BR text .
Compact JSON omits parser metadata. Extended JSON includes the full
internal service result.
.SH PLUGIN LIST OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --output " format"
Set output format. Supported values are
.BR text ,
.BR json ,
and
.BR json-extended .
The default is
.BR text .
JSON returns
.BR rootDirectoryPath ,
.BR registryPath ,
and a
.B plugins
array with each registration's
.BR src ,
.BR origin ,
.BR sig ,
and
.BR version .
Extended JSON also preserves additional registration fields.
.TP
.BI --format " format"
Alias for
.BR --output .
When either option is repeated, the last value wins.
.SH RESOLVE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --root " path"
Set the resolution root directory. Relative
.B /
paths in specs are resolved from this root. The default is the current
directory.
.TP
.BI --section " name"
Include a section by name, or
.BR all .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI --sections " names"
Include comma-separated section names, or
.B all
to include every SpecDD section present in each spec.
.TP
.BI --depth " depth"
Control how far
.B resolve
expands soft links. The default is
.BR 2 .
Use
.B 0
for vertical context only,
.B 1
for direct links from the target spec only,
.B 2
for target links plus immediate parent context links,
.B 3
to also expand the next parent context level, or
.B all
to recursively follow all reachable links with cycle protection.
.TP
.BI --format " format"
Set output format. Supported values are
.BR text ,
.BR json ,
and
.BR json-extended .
The default is
.BR text .
.SH LINT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --format " format"
Set output format. Supported values are
.BR text
and
.BR json .
The default is
.BR text .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Existing SSH agent socket inherited by Git for plugin access. SSH configuration,
including host aliases and IdentityAgent, and explicit GIT_SSH or GIT_SSH_COMMAND
settings are preserved. Container use requires an accessible agent socket and
SSH configuration and known hosts mounted for the container user; see README
for a Linux Docker example. The image provides Git and OpenSSH.
.TP
.B SPECDD_LOG_LEVEL
Set CLI log verbosity. Supported values are
.BR error ,
.BR warning ,
.BR warn ,
.BR log ,
.BR info ,
and
.BR debug .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully. For
.BR check-update ,
exit status
.B 0
also means no update is needed.
.TP
.B 1
The command completed with a user-visible non-success result, such as
an available update from
.B check-update
or lint errors from
.BR lint .
.TP
.B >1
The command failed because of invalid input, missing prerequisites,
download or verification failure, filesystem failure, or another
unexpected error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .specdd/bootstrap.md
Project bootstrap file used to identify local SpecDD framework version
and project rules.
.TP
.B .specdd/bootstrap.local.md
Optional local operator overrides. This file is ignored by the
generated
.BR .specdd/.gitignore .
.TP
.B .agents/skills
Project Agent Skills installation directory.
.TP
.B .specdd/plugins.json
Plugin registrations with source, origin, checksum, and requested version.
.TP
.B .specdd/plugins
Managed plugin files grouped by repository coordinates and plugin name.
.TP
.B .specdd/plugins.lock
Exclusive lock held during plugin installation.
.TP
.B ~/.agents/skills
User Agent Skills installation directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize the current directory:
.B specdd init
.TP
Update an existing project:
.B specdd update
.TP
Check whether a newer framework release exists:
.B specdd check-update
.TP
Deploy project Agent Skills:
.B specdd agentskills deploy path/to/project
.TP
Deploy user Agent Skills:
.B specdd agentskills deploy --user
.TP
Install a plugin over SSH using the current agent:
.B specdd plugin add @acme/specdd-plugins review v1.2.0
.TP
List installed plugins as JSON:
.B specdd plugin list --output json
.TP
Update all managed plugins at their recorded versions:
.B specdd plugin update
.TP
Update one plugin to a new version:
.B specdd plugin update @acme/specdd-plugins review v2.0.0
.TP
Inspect selected sections:
.B specdd inspect path/to/project --sections Purpose,Must,Tasks
.TP
Resolve relevant specs with default depth:
.B specdd resolve path/to/project/src/feature --root path/to/project
.TP
Resolve only vertical context:
.B specdd resolve --depth 0 path/to/project/src/feature
.TP
Resolve recursively:
.B specdd resolve --depth all --root path/to/project path/to/project/src/feature
.TP
Lint specs as JSON:
.B specdd lint path/to/project --format json
.SH SEE ALSO
SpecDD documentation:
.UR https://specdd.ai
.UE
